From 9c0f2d605736663b682aa0e79f56937b4321899b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:31:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Input: synaptics-tcm-spi: wake on double tap and fingerprint
 touch

When the S3910 names a panel, it follows it: with the display off the
controller enters gesture mode and wakes the system on a double tap or a
touch on the fingerprint area. Firmware fingerprint contacts are reported
as a real contact in slot zero; ordinary touches are suppressed in
gesture mode. gesture_state in sysfs reports the mode and event counts.

(cherry picked from commit 86bd5c1dabd43e61dcd53c7120cadc91e80c1bf6)
---
 .../sysfs-driver-synaptics-tcm-gesture        |  12 +
 .../input/touchscreen/syna,s3910.yaml         |   6 +
 drivers/input/touchscreen/Kconfig             |   1 +
 .../input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm_gesture.h |  23 ++
 drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm_spi.c | 299 +++++++++++++++++-
 5 files changed, 338 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-synaptics-tcm-gesture
 create mode 100644 drivers/input/touchscreen/synaptics_tcm_gesture.h

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-synaptics-tcm-gesture b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-synaptics-tcm-gesture
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..d7cedb9bbad0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-synaptics-tcm-gesture
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/spi/devices/.../gesture_state
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
+Description:
+                Read-only mode and event counters for an S3910 following a DRM
+                panel. gesture=1 means the volatile wakeup-gesture, double-tap
+                mask and touch-hold settings were written and read back.
+                reporting=0 indicates setup/recovery or a mode failure.
+                Event counters include only firmware-decoded double taps and
+                FOD contacts; no coordinates or biometric data are exposed.
+                power/wakeup uses the standard device wakeup ABI. The state
+                reports system wake retention separately from display-off.
